messages:
erin: Quick sync after the autoscale RFC merge. We still need a crisp boundary: control-plane issues lightweight prewarm intents, operator subscribes and manages actual node/GPU lifecycle. Proposing a small event-driven surface.

sam: Sounds right. Minimal API: CreatePrewarm(idempotency_key, tenant, slots, ttl, priority, fallback) -> intent_id + status. Keep it async so control-plane doesn't block on operator.

mike: Two failure modes worry me: (1) stampede of prewarms at region peak, (2) operator lag causing tenant timeouts. Solution: per-tenant soft headroom + global reservoir + intent TTL + explicit LeaseTimeout event.

anika: Token-bucket style quotas for tenants + reservoir pool for cross-tenant bursts. Make reservoir configurable by org/region and link to billing bucket so finance can cap spend. Decouple acceptance from billing check.

erin: Important: operator should emit events: LeaseAccepted, LeaseRejected(reason), LeaseReady, LeaseExpired. Control-plane listens and routes traffic or applies fallback_model when lease not Ready.

ops-bot: infra: autoscaler-canary v1.14 deployed to canary-eu-west (log: /deploy/2833337777).

sam: Observability minimal set: intent_created, intent_accepted, intent_rejected, intent_ready, intent_timed_out. Tag with region/org/tenant and include p95 admission latency + time_to_ready.

mike: Add metrics the operator exposes: inflight_prewarms, reclaimable_intents, current_gpu_util, reservoir_available. Use p95/p99 for throttles.

anika: For rollout: operator shim that translates legacy reserve calls into intents. Dual-write for 2 weeks in canary, compare metrics, then flip. Will draft OpenAPI + rollback steps.

erin: Proto sketch for doc: ```proto
message CreatePrewarm {
  string idempotency_key = 1;
  string tenant_id = 2;
  int32 slots = 3;
  int64 ttl_seconds = 4;
  enum Priority { LOW=0; NORMAL=1; HIGH=2; }
  Priority priority = 5;
  string fallback_model = 6;
  int32 fallback_slots = 7;
}
message PrewarmReply {
  string intent_id = 1;
  enum Status { PENDING=0; ACCEPTED=1; REJECTED=2; }
  Status status = 2;
  string reason = 3;
}
```

mike: Also recommend speculative soft-warm with short TTL and immediate reclaim path to reduce cold-starts. Operator must publish reclaimable_intents metric and support forced_cancel. Chaos tests should include operator crash and delayed reclaim.

sam: Add retry/backoff guidance: exponential backoff + jitter on quota rejection to avoid synchronous retries.

anika: I'll add failure-mode test cases: operator-unresponsive, metering outage (shouldn't block acceptance), reservoir exhaustion, overlapping intents from same tenant.

erin: Agreement check: soft headroom per-tenant + shared reservoir + idempotent async intents + operator shim for rollout. Any objections?

sam: None, thumbs up. :thumbsup:

mike: LGTM. :+1:

anika: Okay, starting the OpenAPI draft and test plan. :ok_hand:

erin: Thanks all — I'll fold this into the RFC and post update with timeline and chaos tests. Ping me if you want to be on the rollout call.
